==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{m|la|proximatus}}, past participle of {{m|la|proximare||to draw near, approach}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|proximus||nearest}}, superlative of {{m|la|prope||near}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# [[close|Close]] or [[closest]]; [[adjacent]].
#* J. S. Harford
#*: '''proximate''' ancestors
#* T. Burnet
#*: the '''proximate''' natural causes of it [the deluge]
# {{lb|en|legal}} Immediately preceding or following in a chain of causation.
# About to take place; [[impending]].

====Antonyms====
